Package: jmv2gg
Title: Editable Publication Figures from Jamovi Analysis Code
Version: 0.2.6
Authors@R: person("Gilad", "Feldman", email = "giladfel@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Converts jamovi and ggstatsplot analysis code into explicit,
    editable ggplot2 and BetterGG code. Preserves existing R Markdown analyses,
    adds publication figure exports, and prepares enhanced HTML reports.
    Conversion parses code without executing it and can run locally in WebR.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.5.0)
Imports: jsonlite, yaml, BetterGG (>= 0.2.3)
Suggests: ggplot2, emmeans, car, afex, haven, ragg, ggdist, ggrepel, ggside, ggsignif, patchwork,
    statsExpressions, styler, jmv, psych, ggstatsplot,
    rmarkdown, knitr, markdown, jmvcore, testthat (>= 3.0.0), withr, png, callr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
URL: https://github.com/giladfeldman/jmv2gg
BugReports: https://github.com/giladfeldman/jmv2gg/issues
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
Remotes: giladfeldman/BetterGG@19f7562d89a3ecfd82518a4a1831c34bf96b20bd
